<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="3b2f5225">&lt;p&gt;
    Project resources complete the work assignments for the project in support of work defined in the PMP in order to
    achieve project objectives. Tools and techniques&amp;nbsp;suggested by PMBOK to integrate people and activities include
    interpersonal skills, training, team-building activities, ground rules, co-location meetings, and recognition and
    rewards. A brief description of each is provided.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Interpersonal skills use “soft” skills such as empathy, influence, leadership and creativity to encourage
        cooperation and reduce problems
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Training enhances the competencies of team members via formal or informal training (e.g., classroom, on-the-job,
        mentoring and coaching)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Team-building activities provide opportunities to solidify the team through status review meetings, team
        checkpoints, an off-site event, or other activity aimed towards improving interpersonal relationships and helping
        team members work well together
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ground rules establish clear expectations regarding acceptable team member behavior
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Co-location meetings involve assembling all or most of the team members virtually or in the same physical location
        to enhance their work as a team
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Recognition and rewards provide incentives to recognize and reward individuals for desirable behavior and to
        demonstrate that individuals are valued&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
